# ASUS K53SC - function row defaults to the printed media/brightness keys
#
# The keys carry media icons, and the Fn layer cannot be used: Fn+F5 and Fn+F6
# emit the identical scancode pair (0x23 then 0x14), so no keymap can tell them
# apart. An Apple-style "Fn inverts the row" scheme is impossible on this
# keyboard. Instead the plain row does the printed functions by default, and
# `k53sc-fnrow toggle` flips it to real F1-F12 when you need them.
#
# Background: this unit's EC adjusts brightness privately via LCD_BL_PWM and
# never raises the _Q0E/_Q0F ACPI queries stock's DSDT declares - they are
# vestigial here. Under coreboot the GPU drives the panel, so routing the
# keypress to intel_backlight is the working path.
#
# F1/F2 are deliberately NOT remapped: sleep and wifi-kill are destructive if
# hit by accident (mid-game, say). They stay available on Fn+F1 / Fn+F2, which
# reach the EC ACPI/WMI path independently of this keymap.
# F3/F4 are unlabelled on this unit and are left as ordinary function keys.

evdev:atkbd:dmi:bvn*:bvr*:bd*:svnASUSTeKComputerInc.:pnK53SC:*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3f=brightnessdown
 KEYBOARD_KEY_40=brightnessup
 KEYBOARD_KEY_41=display_off
 KEYBOARD_KEY_42=switchvideomode
 KEYBOARD_KEY_43=touchpad_toggle
 KEYBOARD_KEY_44=mute
 KEYBOARD_KEY_57=volumedown
 KEYBOARD_KEY_58=volumeup
